  "summary": "Centralia (WA) Police Department will continue using its Flock Safety ALPR cameras despite new state restrictions under SB 6002, though it will lose three cameras located within 500 feet of protected sites (a school, library, and Planned Parenthood) and adapt to shorter retention and felony/gross-misdemeanor-only use limits. The article contrasts Centralia's continued use with Seattle, Kent, and Pierce County agencies that temporarily shut off their systems to comply.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "we complied with the law, but we found new tactics.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "The Centralia Police Department has three cameras that violated that rule that have since been shut off.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "I think it's absolutely foolish to say that we're not going to have Flock cameras around schools",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    }
